- `SpawnListInput.status` still accepts `queued` and `finalizing` on the extension and MCP
  surfaces, while `spawn list` rejects them as filters. Those surfaces never
  warned about the values, so deprecate them there for one release before rejecting them.
- `ops/work_sessions.py:work_session_chat_ids` builds its active chat set from any
  active session attached to the work item, which is wider than `spawn_work_id` in
  `ops/work_membership.py` (active primaries plus recorded child work ids): a child
  session that switches items still counts. The wider rule is `work sessions`' existing
  behavior, so folding it into the shared helper would change that command's output.
  Jimmy owns that product decision; record it here when made.
- `work show`, `spawn list --work` and the dashboard still spend most of their time on
  session reads. On a runtime with a 98 MB `sessions.jsonl` (~59k events),
  `active_session_work_ids` replays it on every call (~200-365 ms) and
  `work_session_chat_ids` plus the index's `sessions()` take about 0.9 s. Narrow or
  cache the session read rather than adding a parallel fast path.
